WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:03.128
Kind of cool that we get to make a movie.

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:06.423
Kind of really, really crazy that we get to make a movie.

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:08.550
I kind of have to pinch myself everyday.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.426
Do you need one now?

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:11.428
Yeah, can you? Would you?

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:11.886
Real?

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.638
Is it? I don't know.

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.267
I'm Grace Kaufman, and I play Lennie Walker.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:20.020
Hey, my name is Jacques Colimon. I play Joe Fontaine.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.858
Can I ask you a question?

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.568
Please, please do.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:28.737
What did you do when you found out you got the role?

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:33.324
I just felt the most honored that I was chosen to play a role 

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:36.786
that meant so much to me, and then I started crying.

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:37.871
Like ugly crying? Or like...

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.248
Like ugly crying. Like the ugliest that it gets.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:41.332
You like Lennie?

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.417
I like her a lot.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:45.712
I really love her passion for things.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.338
You think you'd be friends with her in real life?

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.381
I think so.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:54.220
As somebody who has had their fair share of grief and coming to terms with loss

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.015
we would get along because there's a mutual understanding there.

00:00:57.348 --> 00:00:58.308
That's really beautiful.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:00:59.142
Oh thanks. 

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.894
I've said too much.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:05.523
Lennie has trepidation with playing clarinet, right?

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:08.443
Yeah, especially after she loses Bailey.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:11.780
She finds it really hard to pursue the things that she's passionate about.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.074
It's really challenging for her to find that momentum

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.409
to play the clarinet how she used to.

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:18.661
Clarinet is a hard instrument.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:23.083
Lennie blows my mind how she's able to play 

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:26.044
something that's so challenging so flawlessly.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.170
But you do it too. 

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.380
Yeah, but I had to learn clarinet for this role.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.800
I thought you told me that you were playing clarinet for like ten years.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.468
Oh, uh...

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.178
Is that what I said?

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.846
Look at this.

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:38.515
Come on, this way.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.183
Are you excited to get out in these woods?

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.267
I mean who wouldn't?

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.229
These trees are like over a thousand years old.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.439
We're so lucky we just get to frolic in this.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.817
That's like basically what we get to do.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:50.944
It's like the trees are talking.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.612
What are they saying to you?

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:58.993
Look at me. The all beautiful in the way that is shiny and green.

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:01.246
What's your favorite moment on set?

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:08.128
Individually with each person I've had such heartfelt and hilarious moments.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.588
It's been really special.

